I hoisted `profile` into a local and marked the null check as unlikely so the hot profile-lookup path stays fall-through with fewer redundant loads; the logic and results are unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 t = type;
    if (t != FIT_UINT8_INVALID)
        return t;

    const auto* p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect(p == 0, 0) || profileIndex >= p->numFields)
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[profileIndex].type;
}
```